;
; DEED clause profile: AGENTIC.deed, v1.0.0 (DRAFT)
; Prose and rationale: docs/estate-reconciliation/A7-contractiles-descriptiles-anchor.adoc
; sections 7.1, 7.2 (the AGENTIC.deed row) and 14.2 (J19, the settings
; interface); rulings J4, J14, J19, J20 and J33 of 2026-11-14 (the chora's
; (agentic …) moves here whole). Field sources:
; 1-formats/deed/mappings/agentic-neurosym-playbook-to-repo-deed.adoc and
; docs/DESCRIPTILE-SPEC.adoc (AGENTIC). M3 module order: section 11.
;
; A CLAUSE PROFILE, not a new grammar. Every rule below is also a `field` or
; `clause` of deed.abnf v2.0.0, so AGENTIC.deed still passes deed_lint
; unchanged. Rules it borrows: string, symbol, boolean, integer and token-sep
; are deed.abnf's; date-string and symbol-list are common.abnf's. Requires
; RFC 7405 (%s"..." case-sensitive literals).
;
; Where it applies: AGENTIC.deed (head descriptile-deed, J14), at the top level
; of the form. Every member is optional. SEMANTIC (validator-enforced,
; deed_lint.js --agentic):
;   * the descriptile header, as for every descriptile (J20, J28, J4, YD06);
;   * each agentic-field at most once, and at most one of each clause;
;   * no model pin and no language allow or ban list (YD04, YL3), and no
;     (rule …) (YF02);
;   * the J19 journal: see ag-relaxation;
;   * with the chora deed read alongside, a chora (agentic …) is warned, and
;     refused in strict mode (J33, YF05).

agentic-field   = ( %s":version"          token-sep string )
                / ( %s":last-updated"     token-sep date-string )
                / ( %s":tools"            token-sep symbol-list )
                / ( %s":project-specific" token-sep string )
                ; :version and :last-updated come from the chora's (agentic …)
                ; (J33); :tools and :project-specific are A7 7.2's. :tools
                ; names tool classes, never a model (YD04).
                ; SEMANTIC: the strings are not empty.

ag-patterns     = "(" %s"patterns" 1*(token-sep pattern-member) [token-sep] ")"
pattern-member  = ( %s":code-review"   token-sep string )
                / ( %s":refactoring"   token-sep string )
                / ( %s":testing"       token-sep string )
                / ( %s":documentation" token-sep string )
                ; DESCRIPTILE-SPEC: the per-activity posture.

ag-permissions  = "(" %s"permissions" 1*(token-sep permission-member) [token-sep] ")"
permission-member = ( %s":source"       token-sep boolean )
                  / ( %s":tests"        token-sep boolean )
                  / ( %s":docs"         token-sep boolean )
                  / ( %s":config"       token-sep boolean )
                  / ( %s":create-files" token-sep boolean )

ag-integrity    = "(" %s"integrity" 1*(token-sep integrity-member) [token-sep] ")"
integrity-member = ( %s":fail-closed"                      token-sep boolean )
                 / ( %s":require-evidence-per-step"        token-sep boolean )
                 / ( %s":allow-silent-skip"                token-sep boolean )
                 / ( %s":require-rerun-after-fix"          token-sep boolean )
                 / ( %s":release-claim-requires-hard-pass" token-sep boolean )
                 ; Carried verbatim, #f included: a flipped allow-silent-skip
                 ; is how a silent skip escapes (mapping section 3).

ag-methodology  = "(" %s"methodology" 1*(token-sep methodology-member) [token-sep] ")"
methodology-member = ( %s":instructions-dir"    token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":instructions-clause" token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":default-mode"        token-sep symbol )
                   ; :instructions-dir is a repo-relative path (the mapping);
                   ; :instructions-clause names a chora clause (the template:
                   ; "bot-directives"). SEMANTIC: at most one of the two.

ag-hooks        = "(" %s"hooks" 1*(token-sep hook-member) [token-sep] ")"
hook-member     = ( %s":on-enter"  token-sep string )
                / ( %s":on-exit"   token-sep string )
                / ( %s":on-commit" token-sep string )
                ; The mapping's ruled row (2026-10-27).
                ; SEMANTIC (every clause above): each member at most once,
                ; and the clause is not empty.

ag-settings     = "(" %s"settings" token-sep ag-affirmation *(token-sep ag-relaxation) [token-sep] ")"
                ; J19 (14.2). The (affirmation …) clause comes first and gives
                ; the starting policy; each (relaxation …) after it is one
                ; journal entry.
ag-affirmation  = "(" %s"affirmation" token-sep %s":may-change" token-sep symbol-list
                  token-sep %s":report-to" token-sep symbol-list [token-sep] ")"
                ; Who may change the setting and where a change is reported.
                ; It never holds the value, which starts as required: a clause
                ; alone can never relax affirmation (J19). A party is owner,
                ; agent or a named role; a channel is a symbol.
ag-relaxation   = "(" %s"relaxation" 1*(token-sep relaxation-member) [token-sep] ")"
relaxation-member = ( %s":seq"         token-sep integer )
                  / ( %s":setting"     token-sep ag-setting )
                  / ( %s":value"       token-sep ( boolean / symbol-list ) )
                  / ( %s":changed-by"  token-sep symbol )
                  / ( %s":changed-on"  token-sep date-string )
                  / ( %s":reported-to" token-sep symbol )
                  / ( %s":receipt"     token-sep string )
ag-setting      = %s"affirmation.required" / %s"affirmation.may-change" / %s"affirmation.report-to"
                ; SEMANTIC (J19): every member exactly once. :value is a
                ; boolean for affirmation.required and a symbol list for the
                ; other two. The :seq values run 1, 2, 3 … in order, with no
                ; gap and no duplicate, or the journal is refused whole. An
                ; entry is refused when :changed-by is not in :may-change, or
                ; :reported-to is not in :report-to, as they stood at the last
                ; accepted state (a change never authorises itself). An
                ; authorised, reported entry is accepted only when its
                ; :receipt verifies with the channel; no channel receipt
                ; interface exists yet, so no entry is accepted and
                ; affirmation stays required (J4 default). Whether the
                ; (affirmation …) clause was edited after it was first set is
                ; checked against the base version (14.2), outside this
                ; profile.
